I walk home through a large park.
An hour ago I was at a museum.
Now I just want to enjoy the good weather.
I stop at a small kiosk to buy a waffle ice cream.
"Here you go, here is your ice cream," the man in the kiosk says.
"Thank you very much," I reply and take the ice cream.
I walk slowly along the lake in the park.
This waffle ice cream looks really good.
Suddenly I hear a loud noise above me.
A large seagull dives right down towards me.
It wants to steal my ice cream!
I duck quickly and shield my ice cream with my hand.
The bird is not going to steal my food.
The seagull flies past and lands on the grass.
A woman on a bench laughs.
"They are very cheeky today," she says.
"Yes, they certainly are," I laugh back.
I quickly finish eating my ice cream while I walk on.
